.TH AUGUR 1 2026-10-04 "Augur @version@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
augur \- ask Augur, the desktop's AI service, from the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B augur status
.br
.B augur profiles
.br
.B augur models
.RI [ PROFILE ]
.br
.B augur classify
.B \-q
.I FILE
.RB [ \-p
.IR PROFILE ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR MODEL ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RI [ INPUT ...]
.br
.B augur usage
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR WHEN ]
.RB [ \-\-until
.IR WHEN ]
.RB [ \-\-by
.IR KEYS ]
.RB [ \-\-app
.IR ID ]
.br
.B augur ask
.RB [ \-p
.IR PROFILE ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR MODEL ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR TIER ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR SYSTEM ]
.RB [ \-\-schema
.IR JSON | @FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-tools
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-rounds
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-stream ]
.RB [ \-\-app\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RI [ PROMPT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Augur is a session D\-Bus service
.RB ( augurd ,
.BR org.gemwm.Augur )
that gives desktop programs AI without each of them talking to AI
providers: it knows the providers, the keys, and which model to use.
.B augur
asks it over D\-Bus, as any program would.
D\-Bus starts
.B augurd
when it's first asked.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Whether Augur is on, the config it read, the default profile, and why
it's off if it is.
Exits 1 when it's off.
.TP
.B profiles
The profiles in the config, each with its provider and tiers, and what's
wrong with any that can't be used.
.TP
.BR models " [\fIPROFILE\fR]"
The models the profile's provider lists (the default profile's if none
is named).
.TP
.BR classify " \fB\-q\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT\fR...]"
Asks questions about the input (stdin when it isn't given) and prints
each answer.
.I FILE
is a JSON object of questions by name, each with a
.B type
.RB ( choice ", " yes\-no
or
.BR score ),
.BR instructions ,
and for a choice its
.B options
(an object of names and what they mean), for a yes\-no what counts as
.B yes
and
.B no
if it helps, and for a score its
.B levels
(an array, lowest first).
A profile with a
.B classifier
answers with probabilities; one without, with its chat model.
.B \-\-json
prints the answers as JSON;
.B \-v
says what answered.
.TP
.BR usage " [\fIOPTIONS\fR]"
Requests, tokens and what they cost, from the log: this month's, by
program, unless the options say otherwise.
.I WHEN
is
.BR today ", " yesterday ", " week
(the last seven days),
.B month
(since the 1st),
.BR year ", " all ,
or a date,
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD ;
.B \-\-until
isn't included.
.B \-\-by
adds up by
.BR app ", " profile ", " model
or
.BR day ,
or several with commas, or
.BR none .
A cost is what the provider said it charged, or the tokens at the
profile's
.BI price. MODEL
from the config; requests with neither are counted as unpriced.
.TP
.BR ask " [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR...]"
Asks, and prints the answer as it's written.
The prompt is the arguments, or stdin when there are none.
.SH OPTIONS FOR ASK
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-profile " PROFILE"
The profile to ask, instead of the program's or the default one.
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-model " MODEL"
The model, by the provider's name for it.
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-tier " TIER"
The model the profile gives this tier, such as
.B smart
or
.BR cheap .
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-system " TEXT"
A system prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-schema " JSON\fR|\fP@FILE"
Answer in JSON matching this JSON Schema, given as it is or read from
.IR FILE .
The answer is checked, and asked for once more if it doesn't match.
.TP
.BI \-\-tools " FILE"
Offer the model tools.
.I FILE
is a JSON array of objects with a
.BR name ,
a
.BR description ,
a
.B schema
(a JSON Schema for the arguments, an object) and a
.BR command .
A call's arguments go to the command, run by
.BR sh (1),
on stdin; what it prints is the result.
If it fails, what it printed to stderr is why, and the model is told.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-rounds " N"
Turns the model gets with tools before it must answer without them
(8).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stream
Print the answer when it's all there.
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-id " ID"
Ask as this program, for its
.B [app]
settings in the config.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
On stderr: the profile and model that answered, the tokens, and the tool
calls.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/augur/config
has the profiles: a provider
.RB ( openai ", " anthropic ", " openrouter ", " cloudflare ", " ollama
or
.BR openai\-compatible ),
how to get its key, its model and its tiers; and per program settings.
It's read again when it changes.
See the README for all of it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/augur/config
The configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/augur/log
What was asked of whom: app, profile, model, tokens and cost, never the
text.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AUGUR_DISABLED
Set to anything but 0 in
.BR augurd 's
environment, Augur is off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when Augur failed or is off; 2 for a mistake on the
command line; 130 when interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
augur ask "Why is the sky blue?"
augur ask \-p anthropic \-t smart \-s "Be brief." "What's a monad?"
echo "I lost my keys" | augur ask \-\-schema \e
    '{"type":"object","properties":{"mood":{"enum":["happy","sad"]}}}'
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR busctl (1),
.UR https://github.com/matthewp/augur
.UE
